/** 英文字典：易經 64 卦卦名（拼音 · 意譯（上卦 over 下卦））、卦辭簡解，以及 384 爻英譯（L10N.ICHING_YAO：[原文英譯, 白話英譯] ×6，爻題由 deep-readings.js 產生） */
L10N.add({
  "乾為天": "Qian · The Creative (Heaven over Heaven)",
  "創始亨通，剛健中正。萬物資始，君子以自強不息。事業開創之象。": "Creative origin and sublime success; strong, firm, central and upright. All things owe their beginning to it, and the superior person strengthens himself ceaselessly. A sign of launching a great undertaking.",
  "坤為地": "Kun · The Receptive (Earth over Earth)",
  "柔順包容，厚德載物。君子以厚德載物。宜守不宜攻，穩健為上。": "Yielding and receptive, embracing all. The superior person carries all things with generous virtue. Better to hold steady than to push forward; stability comes first.",
  "水雷屯": "Zhun · Difficult Beginnings (Water over Thunder)",
  "萬物始生，艱難重重。創業初期多阻礙，須有耐心逐步克服。": "All things are just being born, amid many hardships. The early days of a venture meet many obstacles; be patient and overcome them step by step.",
  "山水蒙": "Meng · Youthful Folly (Mountain over Water)",
  "蒙昧未明，啟發教育。宜求教於人，不宜自以為是。": "Youthful ignorance, awaiting enlightenment and education. Seek guidance from others; do not presume you know best.",
  "水天需": "Xu · Waiting (Water over Heaven)",
  "等待時機，飲食宴樂。機緣將至，耐心守候即可。": "Waiting for the right moment, with food and drink and good cheer. Opportunity is approaching; simply wait patiently.",
  "天水訟": "Song · Conflict (Heaven over Water)",
  "爭訟衝突，慎言謹行。宜和解不宜對抗，退一步海闊天空。": "Disputes and conflict; be careful in word and deed. Seek reconciliation rather than confrontation. Take a step back and the world opens up.",
  "地水師": "Shi · The Army (Earth over Water)",
  "興師動眾，戰爭之象。宜以柔克剛，不可輕舉妄動。": "Mobilizing the troops, an image of war. Overcome hardness with softness; do not act rashly.",
  "水地比": "Bi · Holding Together (Water over Earth)",
  "親附和合，團結互助。人際關係和諧，合作共贏之象。": "Drawing close and uniting, standing together in mutual support. Harmonious relationships, an image of cooperation where everyone wins.",
  "風天小畜": "Xiao Chu · Small Taming (Wind over Heaven)",
  "小有積蓄，逐漸成長。雖有小成，仍需持續努力。": "Small savings, gradual growth. Though there is some small success, continued effort is still needed.",
  "天澤履": "Lü · Treading (Heaven over Lake)",
  "履行實踐，如履薄冰。謹慎行事，步步為營。": "Treading the path and putting things into practice, as if walking on thin ice. Act with caution and advance step by step.",
  "地天泰": "Tai · Peace (Earth over Heaven)",
  "天地交泰，萬事亨通。陰陽和合，事業順利，家庭和睦。": "Heaven and earth unite in peace, and all things go smoothly. Yin and yang are in harmony; career goes well and the family lives in concord.",
  "天地否": "Pi · Standstill (Heaven over Earth)",
  "天地不交，閉塞不通。宜守不宜攻，韜光養晦。": "Heaven and earth do not meet; all is blocked and nothing gets through. Better to hold steady than to push forward; keep a low profile.",
  "天火同人": "Tong Ren · Fellowship (Heaven over Fire)",
  "志同道合，團結一心。適合組團隊、談合作、交朋友。": "Sharing the same aims and ideals, united in one heart. Good for building teams, negotiating partnerships and making friends.",
  "火天大有": "Da You · Great Possession (Fire over Heaven)",
  "大有所獲，豐收之象。事業鼎盛，名利雙收。": "Great gains, an image of abundant harvest. Career at its height, with both fame and fortune.",
  "地山謙": "Qian · Modesty (Earth over Mountain)",
  "謙虛受益，滿招損。為人謙和，運勢亨通持久。": "Modesty brings benefit; fullness invites loss. Be humble and gentle, and good fortune will flow smoothly and last.",
  "雷地豫": "Yu · Enthusiasm (Thunder over Earth)",
  "愉悅安樂，順勢而為。宜享受當下，但勿過度放縱。": "Joy and ease; go with the flow of events. Enjoy the present moment, but do not overindulge.",
  "澤雷隨": "Sui · Following (Lake over Thunder)",
  "隨順時勢，靈活應變。勿固執己見，順其自然。": "Follow the times and adapt flexibly. Don't cling to your own views; let things take their natural course.",
  "山風蠱": "Gu · Repairing Decay (Mountain over Wind)",
  "積弊腐壞，革新整頓。宜清理舊問題，重新出發。": "Accumulated decay calls for reform and renewal. Clear up old problems and make a fresh start.",
  "地澤臨": "Lin · Approach (Earth over Lake)",
  "居高臨下，監督管理。領導力佳，適合督導他人。": "Overseeing from above, supervising and managing. Strong leadership — well suited to guiding others.",
  "風地觀": "Guan · Contemplation (Wind over Earth)",
  "觀察學習，靜觀其變。宜多聽多看，不急於表態。": "Observe and learn; watch quietly as things unfold. Listen and look more, and don't rush to take a stand.",
  "火雷噬嗑": "Shi He · Biting Through (Fire over Thunder)",
  "咬合障礙，清除阻撓。宜果斷處理問題。": "Biting through obstacles and clearing away what blocks the way. Deal with problems decisively.",
  "山火賁": "Bi · Grace (Mountain over Fire)",
  "文飾美化，注重外表。宜提升形象、裝飾門面。": "Adornment and refinement, attention to appearances. A good time to polish your image and present yourself well.",
  "山地剝": "Bo · Splitting Apart (Mountain over Earth)",
  "剝落衰敗，順勢而止。不宜冒進，保存實力。": "Stripping away and decline; stop and go with the trend. Don't push ahead — conserve your strength.",
  "地雷復": "Fu · Return (Earth over Thunder)",
  "一陽來復，否極泰來。冬天將盡，春天不遠。": "One yang line returns; after the worst comes the turn for the better. Winter is ending and spring is not far away.",
  "天雷無妄": "Wu Wang · Innocence (Heaven over Thunder)",
  "真實無妄，順其自然。不可投機取巧，腳踏實地。": "Genuine and free of falsehood; let things follow their natural course. Don't look for shortcuts — keep your feet on the ground.",
  "山天大畜": "Da Chu · Great Taming (Mountain over Heaven)",
  "大積蓄，厚積薄發。宜長期投資，培養實力。": "Great accumulation; build up deeply and release with restraint. Good for long-term investment and building real strength.",
  "山雷頤": "Yi · Nourishment (Mountain over Thunder)",
  "頤養生息，養精蓄銳。注重健康，修身養性。": "Nourishment and rest; restore your energy and gather your strength. Look after your health and cultivate yourself.",
  "澤風大過": "Da Guo · Great Excess (Lake over Wind)",
  "過度極端，超出負荷。量力而行，不可勉強。": "Going to extremes, beyond what can be borne. Act within your means; don't force things.",
  "坎為水": "Kan · The Abysmal (Water over Water)",
  "重重險阻，危機四伏。須有堅定信念，渡過難關。": "Danger upon danger, threats on every side. Hold to firm conviction to get through the hard times.",
  "離為火": "Li · The Clinging (Fire over Fire)",
  "光明依附，熱情照耀。宜保持正向、發揮所長。": "Light that clings and shines warmly. Stay positive and make the most of your strengths.",
  "澤山咸": "Xian · Influence (Lake over Mountain)",
  "感應交流，心靈相通。感情運佳，適合談情說愛。": "Mutual influence and exchange; hearts in tune. Good for romance — a fine time to fall in love.",
  "雷風恆": "Heng · Duration (Thunder over Wind)",
  "恆久不變，持之以恆。適合長期規劃、穩定發展。": "Lasting and unchanging; persistence over time. Good for long-term planning and steady growth.",
  "天山遯": "Dun · Retreat (Heaven over Mountain)",
  "退隱韜光，避開鋒芒。暫時退讓，保全自身。": "Withdraw and conceal your light, stepping aside from the sharp edge of things. Yield for now to keep yourself safe.",
  "雷天大壯": "Da Zhuang · Great Power (Thunder over Heaven)",
  "強壯有力，氣勢如虹。但勿過度強勢，注意分寸。": "Strong and vigorous, with momentum like a rainbow. But do not overplay your strength; keep a sense of measure.",
  "火地晉": "Jin · Progress (Fire over Earth)",
  "晉升進步，前途光明。事業上升期，宜積極進取。": "Promotion and progress, with a bright road ahead. A rising period in your career; be proactive and press forward.",
  "地火明夷": "Ming Yi · Darkening of the Light (Earth over Fire)",
  "光明受損，韜光養晦。逆境中保持希望，等待黎明。": "The light is wounded; hide your brilliance and bide your time. Keep hope in adversity and wait for the dawn.",
  "風火家人": "Jia Ren · The Family (Wind over Fire)",
  "家庭和睦，親情溫暖。適合處理家務、修復關係。": "Harmony at home and the warmth of family. A good time for household matters and mending relationships.",
  "火澤睽": "Kui · Opposition (Fire over Lake)",
  "背離不合，意見分歧。宜求同存異，勿強求一致。": "Estrangement and disagreement, with diverging views. Seek common ground while accepting differences; do not force agreement.",
  "水山蹇": "Jian · Obstruction (Water over Mountain)",
  "艱難困苦，舉步維艱。宜尋求協助，不可孤軍奮戰。": "Hardship and difficulty, where every step is a struggle. Seek help; do not fight alone.",
  "雷水解": "Xie · Deliverance (Thunder over Water)",
  "困難解除，雲開見日。問題終於解決，迎來轉機。": "Difficulties are released and the sun breaks through the clouds. The problem is finally solved and a turning point arrives.",
  "山澤損": "Sun · Decrease (Mountain over Lake)",
  "減損消耗，適度取捨。宜節制開支、減少不必要的消耗。": "Decrease and depletion; weigh what to keep and what to give up. Rein in spending and cut unnecessary waste.",
  "風雷益": "Yi · Increase (Wind over Thunder)",
  "增益成長，日新又新。適合學習進修、開拓新領域。": "Increase and growth, renewing day after day. A good time for study, self-improvement, and opening new fields.",
  "澤天夬": "Guai · Breakthrough (Lake over Heaven)",
  "決斷果敢，當機立斷。面臨抉擇時要果斷但不能莽撞。": "Resolute and decisive, acting the moment it counts. When facing a choice, be decisive but not reckless.",
  "天風姤": "Gou · Coming to Meet (Heaven over Wind)",
  "偶然相遇，機緣巧合。一個意外的相遇可能帶來改變。": "A chance meeting, a lucky coincidence. An unexpected encounter may bring change.",
  "澤地萃": "Cui · Gathering Together (Lake over Earth)",
  "聚集薈萃，人才匯聚。適合組織活動、召集人群。": "Gathering together, where talent assembles. A good time to organize events and bring people together.",
  "地風升": "Sheng · Pushing Upward (Earth over Wind)",
  "步步高升，逐漸向上。事業穩步發展，日漸進步。": "Rising step by step, steadily upward. Your career develops steadily and improves day by day.",
  "澤水困": "Kun · Oppression (Lake over Water)",
  "困境束縛，有志難伸。保持信心，困境不會永久。": "Bound by hardship, unable to realize your ambitions. Keep your faith; the hard times will not last forever.",
  "水風井": "Jing · The Well (Water over Wind)",
  "井養不窮，取之不盡。宜守住根本，穩定中求發展。": "The well nourishes without end, never running dry. Hold on to your roots and grow from a place of stability.",
  "澤火革": "Ge · Revolution (Lake over Fire)",
  "變革創新，破舊立新。適合改變現狀、轉換跑道。": "Revolution and innovation: clear away the old and establish the new. A good time to change the status quo or switch tracks.",
  "火風鼎": "Ding · The Cauldron (Fire over Wind)",
  "鼎新革故，權威穩固。事業穩固，權力地位提升。": "The cauldron: establishing the new and discarding the old, with authority made secure. Your career is stable, and your power and standing rise.",
  "震為雷": "Zhen · The Arousing (Thunder over Thunder)",
  "震動驚嚇，臨危不亂。突發事件中保持冷靜。": "Shock and alarm: staying composed in the face of danger. Keep calm when something sudden happens.",
  "艮為山": "Gen · Keeping Still (Mountain over Mountain)",
  "停止安穩，適可而止。該停就停，知足常樂。": "Stopping and keeping still: know when enough is enough. Stop when it is time to stop; contentment brings happiness.",
  "風山漸": "Jian · Gradual Progress (Wind over Mountain)",
  "循序漸進，按部就班。不急功近利，穩紮穩打。": "Gradual progress, step by step. Do not chase quick results; advance steadily and surely.",
  "雷澤歸妹": "Gui Mei · The Marrying Maiden (Thunder over Lake)",
  "婚姻嫁娶，結合之象。適合談論婚事、締結關係。": "Marriage and union. A good time to discuss marriage or enter into a committed relationship.",
  "雷火豐": "Feng · Abundance (Thunder over Fire)",
  "豐盛圓滿，如日中天。事業巔峰期，收穫最大的時刻。": "Abundance and fullness, like the sun at its zenith. The peak of your career, the moment of greatest harvest.",
  "火山旅": "Lü · The Wanderer (Fire over Mountain)",
  "旅行漂泊，客居他鄉。適合出差旅遊，異地發展。": "The wanderer, living as a guest far from home. Good for business trips and travel, or developing your prospects in another place.",
  "巽為風": "Xun · The Gentle (Wind over Wind)",
  "柔順謙遜，順風而行。宜聽從建議，勿固執。": "Gentle, yielding, and humble, moving with the wind. Be willing to take advice; do not be stubborn.",
  "兌為澤": "Dui · The Joyous (Lake over Lake)",
  "喜悅交流，人際和諧。適合社交聚會、談判溝通。": "Joyful exchange and harmonious relationships. Good for social gatherings, negotiation, and communication.",
  "風水渙": "Huan · Dispersion (Wind over Water)",
  "渙散分離，重新凝聚。宜重整團隊、收拾散亂。": "Dispersion and separation, then coming together again. A time to rebuild the team and gather up what has scattered.",
  "水澤節": "Jie · Limitation (Water over Lake)",
  "節制有度，適可而止。理財、時間管理皆適宜。": "Restraint in due measure; knowing when enough is enough. Favorable for managing money and time.",
  "風澤中孚": "Zhong Fu · Inner Truth (Wind over Lake)",
  "誠信感孚，真心待人。誠意能感動天地，心想事成。": "Inner truth and sincerity; treating others with an honest heart. Sincerity can move heaven and earth, and your wishes come true.",
  "雷山小過": "Xiao Guo · Small Excess (Thunder over Mountain)",
  "小有過失，勿太苛責。小錯可改，大原則守住。": "Small excesses and minor faults; don't be too hard on yourself. Small mistakes can be corrected, as long as the big principles hold.",
  "水火既濟": "Ji Ji · After Completion (Water over Fire)",
  "大事已成，功德圓滿。但居安思危，慎終如始。": "The great task is accomplished, the work complete. But stay alert to danger in times of peace, and be as careful at the end as at the beginning.",
  "火水未濟": "Wei Ji · Before Completion (Fire over Water)",
  "尚未成功，革命未成。繼續努力，不可半途而廢。": "Not yet successful; the revolution is not yet complete. Keep working at it and do not give up halfway."
});

L10N.ICHING_YAO = {
  1: [
    ["Hidden dragon. Do not act.", "The dragon lies hidden in the deep; the time has not yet come. Keep a low profile and build up your strength rather than acting rashly."],
    ["Dragon appearing in the field. It furthers one to see the great man.", "The dragon appears in the field, and your abilities are starting to be noticed. A good time to call on respected people and seek their support."],
    ["All day long the superior person is creatively active; at nightfall he remains watchful, as if in danger. No blame.", "Work tirelessly all day and stay alert even at night. The situation is risky, but caution keeps you free of mistakes."],
    ["Wavering flight over the depths. No blame.", "You may leap upward or fall back into the depths; either way is open to you. Weigh the timing and circumstances before deciding, and you will make no mistake."],
    ["Flying dragon in the heavens. It furthers one to see the great man.", "The dragon soars in the sky, at the very peak. Talent and timing have come together; pursue your ambitions boldly and work alongside capable people."],
    ["Arrogant dragon. There will be remorse.", "The dragon has flown too high and will come to regret it. What reaches its peak must decline, so know your limits and quit while you are ahead."]
  ],
  2: [
    ["Treading on hoarfrost, solid ice is coming.", "When you step on thin frost, you know hard ice is on its way. Small signs foretell big changes, so prepare early."],
    ["Straight, square, great. Without practice, nothing fails to further.", "Be upright, principled and generous. You need not strain or scheme; everything will work out naturally."],
    ["Hidden brilliance; one can remain persevering. If one serves the king, one seeks no achievement but brings things to completion.", "Keep your virtues inside rather than showing them off, and hold to what is right. When assisting others, do not claim the credit, and things will end well."],
    ["A tied-up sack. No blame, no praise.", "Keep the sack tied tight: be careful with your words and actions. You will earn no praise, but you will invite no trouble either."],
    ["A yellow lower garment. Supreme good fortune.", "The yellow lower garment stands for centeredness and humility. Holding a high position with modesty and a sense of your place brings great fortune."],
    ["Dragons fight in the meadow. Their blood is black and yellow.", "Dragons battle in the open field and their blood is dark and yellow. When yin grows strong enough to contend with yang, both sides are hurt; pull back early."]
  ],
  3: [
    ["Hesitation and hindrance. It furthers one to remain persevering. It furthers one to appoint helpers.", "Progress is halting. Stay put and hold to what is right, lay solid foundations and look for capable helpers."],
    ["Difficulties pile up. Horse and wagon part. He is not a robber; he wants to woo. The maiden is chaste and does not pledge herself. Ten years, then she pledges herself.", "Things are hard and you hesitate, holding back like a rider who will not go on. The one approaching is not an enemy but a suitor; keep to your proper role, and when the time is ripe it will come together. Patience is needed."],
    ["Whoever hunts deer without a forester only loses his way in the forest. The superior person sees the signs and prefers to desist. To go on brings humiliation.", "Chasing deer without a guide only gets you lost in the woods. A wise person reads the signs and gives up; forcing it will bring regret."],
    ["Horse and wagon part. Seek union. To go brings good fortune; everything furthers.", "Though you hesitate on horseback, if you take the initiative to seek partnership, going forward brings good fortune and everything works out."],
    ["Difficulties in blessing. A little perseverance brings good fortune; great perseverance brings misfortune.", "Your benefits are hard to spread widely. Holding to what is right in small matters brings good fortune, but forcing big ones brings misfortune. Act within your means."],
    ["Horse and wagon part. Tears of blood flow.", "Hesitating on horseback, weeping tears of blood. The difficulty has reached its end; change your thinking and look for a new way rather than sinking into sorrow."]
  ],
  4: [
    ["To make a fool develop, it furthers one to apply discipline. The fetters should be removed. To go on in this way brings humiliation.", "At the start of teaching the unenlightened, set rules and use measured discipline. If you simply let things go, there will be regret."],
    ["To bear with fools in kindliness brings good fortune. To take a wife brings good fortune. The son is capable of taking charge of the household.", "Being tolerant of the unenlightened brings good fortune, like marrying a good wife, or like a son who can run the household and take on responsibility."],
    ["Do not take a maiden who, seeing a man of gold, loses possession of herself. Nothing furthers.", "Do not marry a woman who loses her composure the moment she sees a rich man. Keep away from people who forget their principles at the sight of gain."],
    ["Entangled folly brings humiliation.", "Stuck in ignorance and far from good teachers, there is regret. Actively seek instruction rather than shutting yourself off."],
    ["Childlike folly brings good fortune.", "Seeking instruction with the open mind of a child brings good fortune. Setting aside your pride to learn yields the greatest benefit."],
    ["In punishing folly, it does not further one to commit transgressions. It furthers one only to prevent transgressions.", "When teaching with stern methods, do not go so far as to treat the learner like an enemy; use firmness to guard against bad influences from outside."]
  ],
  5: [
    ["Waiting in the meadow. It furthers one to abide in what endures. No blame.", "You wait in the distant outskirts, still far from danger. Keep an even mind and stay steady, and you will make no mistake."],
    ["Waiting on the sand. There is some small gossip. The end brings good fortune.", "You wait on the sandbank, drawing nearer to danger, and some gossip arises. Stay calm, and it will turn out well in the end."],
    ["Waiting in the mud brings about the arrival of the enemy.", "Waiting in the mud, right at the edge of danger, you end up drawing the enemy in. Be especially careful."],
    ["Waiting in blood. Get out of the pit.", "Waiting amid bloodshed, you are already caught in danger. Withdraw as circumstances allow and respond calmly, and you can escape."],
    ["Waiting at meat and drink. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "With food and wine prepared, you wait at ease; holding to what is right brings good fortune. The moment is coming, so there is no need to fret."],
    ["One falls into the pit. Three uninvited guests arrive. Honor them, and in the end there will be good fortune.", "You have fallen into the pit, yet three uninvited guests arrive. Treat them with respect, and things will end well."]
  ],
  6: [
    ["If one does not prolong the affair, there is some small gossip. In the end, good fortune.", "Do not drag the dispute out. There may be some words exchanged, but it will turn out well in the end. Better to stop early."],
    ["One cannot win the dispute, returns home and hides in his town of three hundred households. No calamity.", "Unable to win the dispute, you retreat to your small town, and all three hundred households escape disaster. Recognizing the situation and stepping back keeps everyone safe."],
    ["To live on ancient virtue. Perseverance; danger. In the end, good fortune. If one serves the king, one seeks no achievement.", "Rely on what your forebears built and keep to it. Holding to what is right carries some danger, but it ends well. When assisting others, do not insist on credit."],
    ["One cannot win the dispute, turns back and submits to what is right, changes his attitude. Peace in perseverance brings good fortune.", "Unable to win the dispute, you turn back, follow what is right and change your mind. Settling into the proper path brings good fortune."],
    ["Contending before him brings supreme good fortune.", "A fair judgment of the dispute brings great fortune. With a clear-minded arbiter, the conflict can be resolved."],
    ["Even if one is granted a leather belt, by the end of the morning it will have been snatched away three times.", "Rewards won through litigation will be stripped away three times in a single day. Honors gained by fighting cannot be kept for long."]
  ],
  7: [
    ["An army must set forth in proper order. If the order is not good, misfortune.", "An army must march with discipline, or it meets misfortune whether it wins or loses. Set the rules before you begin."],
    ["In the midst of the army. Good fortune. No blame. The king bestows a triple decoration.", "Holding the central position in the army brings good fortune without blame, and the king honors you again and again. You are trusted and able to shoulder the task."],
    ["Perchance the army carries corpses in the wagon. Misfortune.", "The army may come home carrying its dead: misfortune. Acting on your own authority without the ability to back it up is bound to fail."],
    ["The army retreats. No blame.", "The army falls back and makes camp: no blame. Knowing when to retreat preserves your strength."],
    ["There is game in the field. It furthers one to catch it. No blame. Let the eldest lead the army; the younger transports corpses. Then perseverance brings misfortune.", "There is game in the field, so it is right to set out and strike; the campaign has a just cause. Put an experienced elder in command; if the incompetent are given a role, even holding to what is right brings misfortune."],
    ["The great prince issues commands, founds states and vests families with fiefs. The petty person should not be employed.", "The sovereign issues his commands, rewards merit with titles and estates, but petty people must not be given power. After success, choose your people even more carefully."]
  ],
  8: [
    ["Hold to him in sincerity: no blame. Sincerity like a full earthen bowl; in the end good fortune comes from elsewhere.", "Joining with others in good faith brings no blame. When your sincerity is like a brimming earthen jar, unexpected good fortune will come in the end."],
    ["Hold to him inwardly. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Join with others sincerely, from the heart, and hold to what is right for good fortune. Bonds that come from your true self are the most reliable."],
    ["You hold together with the wrong people.", "You have attached yourself to people you should not. You chose your friends poorly; realize it as early as you can."],
    ["Hold to him outwardly also. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Reach outward to join with the worthy, and hold to what is right for good fortune. Follow those above you who are worth following."],
    ["Manifestation of holding together. In the hunt the king uses beaters on three sides only and forgoes the game that runs off in front. The citizens need no warning. Good fortune.", "Joining together openly and honorably. When the king hunts he leaves one side open and lets the game ahead escape, and the townspeople need not be on guard: good fortune. Generosity wins people's hearts."],
    ["He finds no head for holding together. Misfortune.", "Seeking union without making a beginning, without acting early: misfortune. Once the moment has passed, it is hard to cooperate even if you want to."]
  ],
  9: [
    ["Return to the way. How could there be blame? Good fortune.", "Going back the way you came - what fault is there in that? Good fortune. When you notice you have strayed, turn back promptly."],
    ["He allows himself to be drawn into returning. Good fortune.", "Being led back to the right path together with others brings good fortune. Advance and retreat alongside those who share your goals."],
    ["The spokes burst out of the wagon wheels. Man and wife roll their eyes.", "The wheel comes loose from the axle, and husband and wife turn against each other. When there is discord within, nothing can move forward."],
    ["With sincerity, blood vanishes and fear gives way. No blame.", "Holding sincerity in your heart, worry departs and fear dissolves: no blame. Good faith clears away suspicion."],
    ["With sincerity, loyally attached, one is rich together with one's neighbor.", "Sincere and closely bound, you share your wealth with your neighbors. Sharing good fortune makes cooperation all the more solid."],
    ["The rain comes, there is rest. Virtue is honored and carried to the full. Perseverance brings the woman into danger. The moon is nearly full. If the superior person persists, misfortune.", "The rain has fallen and things have come to rest; accumulated virtue is complete. Even a woman holding to what is right faces danger, and with the moon nearly full, a superior person who sets out now meets misfortune. When things reach their peak, stop."]
  ],
  10: [
    ["Simple conduct. Progress without blame.", "Go forward with a plain, simple heart: no blame. Stay true to your original intentions and do what is yours to do."],
    ["Treading a smooth, level course. The perseverance of a quiet, solitary person brings good fortune.", "Walking a broad, level road, the calm and self-contained person who holds to what is right finds good fortune. Without competing or grabbing, you remain at ease and secure."],
    ["A one-eyed man is able to see, a lame man is able to tread. He treads on the tail of the tiger. The tiger bites the man. Misfortune. Thus does a warrior act on behalf of his great prince.", "Poor of sight yet thinking he sees clearly, lame yet thinking he can walk, he steps on the tiger's tail and is bitten: misfortune. Overreaching beyond your abilities ends in harm."],
    ["He treads on the tail of the tiger, with caution and circumspection. In the end, good fortune.", "Stepping on the tiger's tail but staying wary and careful, you find good fortune in the end. In a dangerous position, great care keeps you safe."],
    ["Resolute conduct. Perseverance with awareness of danger.", "Move forward decisively, but even when holding to what is right, watch out for danger. The higher your position and power, the less you can afford to be stubborn and self-willed."],
    ["Look to your conduct and weigh the favorable signs. When everything is fulfilled, supreme good fortune.", "Look back over the road you have traveled and examine what went well and what went badly. If all has come full circle, great fortune. Be good at reflecting and drawing lessons."]
  ],
  11: [
    ["When ribbon grass is pulled up, the sod comes with it, each according to its kind. Setting forth brings good fortune.", "Pull up the cogon grass and its roots come up together, drawing their own kind along. Advancing together with like-minded people brings good fortune."],
    ["Bearing with the uncultured in gentleness, fording the river with resolution, not neglecting what is distant, not regarding one's companions: thus one walks in the middle way.", "Tolerating what is rough and unrefined, having the courage to wade a river on foot, not forgetting those far away and forming no private cliques - this is how you stay on the middle path. Be both broad-minded and willing to take responsibility."],
    ["No plain without a slope, no going without a return. Perseverance in hardship: no blame. Do not grieve over it; with sincerity, there is blessing in one's sustenance.", "No ground stays level forever, and nothing goes without coming back. Hold to what is right in hard times and there is no blame; do not worry, for sincerity brings its own reward."],
    ["Fluttering down, not boasting of wealth, together with his neighbor, guileless and sincere.", "Coming down lightly to mix with others, not putting on the airs of wealth or rank, you get along with your neighbors with no need for guardedness, trusting one another."],
    ["The sovereign Di Yi gives his younger sister in marriage. This brings blessing and supreme good fortune.", "Di Yi gives his younger sister in marriage and is blessed by it: great fortune. Lowering yourself to form a union brings about something beautiful."],
    ["The wall falls back into the moat. Use no army now. Make your commands known within your own town. Perseverance brings humiliation.", "The city wall collapses back into the moat. Now is no time to send troops; you can only issue orders within your own town, and even holding to what is right brings regret. When peace reaches its peak, stagnation follows, so prepare early."]
  ],
  12: [
    ["When ribbon grass is pulled up, the sod comes with it, each according to its kind. Perseverance brings good fortune and success.", "Pull up the cogon grass and its roots come up together, drawing their own kind along. Holding to what is right brings good fortune and success. In hard times, unite with like-minded people to protect yourselves."],
    ["They bear and endure. For the petty person, good fortune. The great man accepts the standstill; success.", "Being tolerated and going along with those above brings good fortune to the petty person; the superior person should accept the obstruction and keep his integrity, and in the end he will succeed."],
    ["They bear shame.", "Harboring shame. In a position that is not rightfully yours, you can only endure the humiliation."],
    ["He who acts at the command of the highest remains without blame. Those of like mind share in the blessing.", "Acting in accordance with the mandate of heaven brings no blame, and your companions share in the blessing. A turning point has appeared."],
    ["Standstill is giving way. Good fortune for the great man. 'What if it should fail? What if it should fail?' In this way he ties it to a cluster of mulberry shoots.", "The obstruction is coming to an end, and those of virtue find good fortune. But stay constantly alert, saying 'it may yet perish,' and you will be as secure as something tied to a thick clump of mulberry."],
    ["The standstill comes to an end. First standstill, then joy.", "The blockage is overturned: first obstruction, then joy. The hard times are finally over."]
  ],
  13: [
    ["Fellowship with others at the gate. No blame.", "Joining with others as soon as you step out the door: no blame. Approach the wider world with an open heart."],
    ["Fellowship with others in the clan. Humiliation.", "Joining only with those of your own clan brings regret. A circle that is too small and partial cannot accomplish great things."],
    ["He hides weapons in the thicket; he climbs the high hill in front of it. For three years he does not rise up.", "Hiding troops in the undergrowth and climbing a high hill to watch, for three years you dare not make a move. Suspicion leads only to wasted effort."],
    ["He climbs up on his wall but does not attack. Good fortune.", "You scale the other side's wall but do not attack: good fortune. Knowing when to stop leaves room for things to turn around."],
    ["Men bound in fellowship first weep and lament, but afterward they laugh. After great struggles they succeed in meeting.", "Joining with others, first you weep and wail, then you laugh; only after the great army wins do you meet again. Good things take time and trouble, but in the end you are reunited."],
    ["Fellowship with others in the meadow. No remorse.", "Joining with others out in the countryside: no remorse. Though not everything is as you wished, there is nothing to regret."]
  ],
  14: [
    ["No relationship with what is harmful; there is no blame in this. If one remains conscious of difficulty, one remains without blame.", "Have no dealings with what is harmful and you commit no fault; stay watchful in hard times and there is no blame. The early days of prosperity call for the most care."],
    ["A big wagon for loading. One may undertake something. No blame.", "Loaded onto a big wagon, you can travel far: no blame. You are capable of carrying heavy responsibilities."],
    ["A prince offers it to the Son of Heaven. A petty person cannot do this.", "A great lord presents rich gifts at an audience with the Son of Heaven; a petty person cannot do this. Only the virtuous know how to use wealth well."],
    ["He makes a difference between himself and his neighbor. No blame.", "Not becoming complacent about your abundance: no blame. Being wealthy without flaunting it is how you keep it."],
    ["He whose sincerity is accessible, yet dignified, has good fortune.", "Dealing with others in good faith while keeping your dignity brings good fortune. Combine generosity with principle."],
    ["He is blessed by heaven. Good fortune. Nothing that does not further.", "Blessed by heaven: good fortune, and everything goes well. In harmony with heaven and with people, blessings come from above."]
  ],
  15: [
    ["A superior person modest about his modesty may cross the great water. Good fortune.", "The superior person who is modest and more modest still can cross the great river: good fortune. Facing difficulty with humility, you can get things done."],
    ["Modesty that comes to expression. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Your reputation for modesty spreads; holding to what is right brings good fortune. This is modesty that has truly earned its name."],
    ["A superior person of modesty and merit carries things to conclusion. Good fortune.", "Having achieved much yet remaining modest, the superior person sees things through from beginning to end: good fortune. Great accomplishment without claiming the credit."],
    ["Nothing that would not further modesty in movement.", "Everything goes well as you put your modesty into practice. Be respectful toward those above you and yielding toward those below."],
    ["Not boasting of wealth before one's neighbor. It furthers one to attack with force. Nothing that does not further.", "Not presuming on your wealth, you win the support of your neighbors, and it is right to move against those who will not submit; everything goes well. Modesty is not weakness - when it is time to act, act."],
    ["Modesty that comes to expression. It is favorable to set armies marching to chastise one's own city and one's country.", "Your reputation for modesty spreads far, and it is right to send out troops against towns that will not submit. Unite people through humble virtue; only by correcting yourself can you win others over."]
  ],
  16: [
    ["Enthusiasm that expresses itself brings misfortune.", "Getting carried away and broadcasting your own delight brings misfortune. Rein yourself in."],
    ["Firm as a rock. Not a whole day. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Steady as a rock, you act on the signs without waiting for the day to end; holding to what is right brings good fortune. See the large in the small and do not sink into comfort."],
    ["Enthusiasm that looks upward creates remorse. Hesitation brings remorse.", "Looking up to others and flattering them in search of pleasure leads to regret, and putting off change brings still more regret. Do not attach yourself to the powerful."],
    ["The source of enthusiasm. He achieves great things. Doubt not. You gather friends around you as a hair clasp gathers the hair.", "Others find their joy through you, and great gains follow. Have no doubts: friends will gather around you the way a hairpin gathers the hair."],
    ["Persistently ill, and still does not die.", "Long ill, yet never dying. Your situation is constrained; hold to what is right in order to endure."],
    ["Deluded enthusiasm. But if after completion one changes, there is no blame.", "Absorption in pleasure has become settled, but if you can change, there is no blame. Turning back in time can still save the situation."]
  ],
  17: [
    ["The official standard shifts. Perseverance brings good fortune. Going out of the gate to associate with others brings achievement.", "Your former position is shifting; hold to what is right and good fortune follows. Going out and engaging with people brings real results — keep an open mind and step outside."],
    ["Clinging to the youth, one loses the grown man.", "Attaching yourself to a child, you lose the grown man. Don't sacrifice the big thing for the small one — choose carefully whom you follow."],
    ["Clinging to the grown man, one loses the youth. Following, one seeks and obtains. It furthers one to abide in perseverance.", "Attach yourself to the strong man and let the child go; what you seek can be found. Settle down and stay upright — be clear about what to keep and what to give up, and hold to the right path."],
    ["Following brings a catch; perseverance brings misfortune. With sincerity on the way, and with clarity, what blame could there be?", "Following others brings you gains, but holding on to them stubbornly brings misfortune. As long as you are sincere, act rightly and are open and above-board, what fault could there be?"],
    ["Sincere toward the excellent. Good fortune.", "Being sincere toward what is good and worthy brings good fortune. You are choosing the right people and causes to follow."],
    ["Held fast, then following; bound to it further. The king makes offering on the Western Mountain.", "First held fast, then willingly following, then bound more firmly still; the king makes sacrifice on the Western Mountain. Bonds held together by complete sincerity are stable and lasting."]
  ],
  18: [
    ["Mending what the father spoiled. With such a son, the late father is without blame. Danger, but good fortune in the end.", "Repairing the damage left by the father's generation — with a son like this, the forebears bear no blame. There is danger, but it ends in good fortune."],
    ["Mending what the mother spoiled. One cannot be rigidly persevering.", "Repairing the damage left by the mother's generation, you must not be too rigid. Family matters call for a gentle, tactful touch."],
    ["Mending what the father spoiled. A little remorse, but no great blame.", "Repairing the father's faults brings a little regret, but no serious error. You may be a bit forceful, but your direction is right."],
    ["Indulging what the father spoiled. Going on brings humiliation.", "Being lenient with the faults of the previous generation will lead to regret if it continues. Problems like this must not be put off."],
    ["Mending what the father spoiled. One wins praise.", "Repairing the father's faults wins you praise. Reform carried out with gentleness and virtue earns recognition."],
    ["He serves neither king nor lord; he holds his own affairs high.", "Not serving kings or lords, he devotes himself to his higher purpose. Step back once the work is done and keep your integrity intact."]
  ],
  19: [
    ["Approaching through mutual feeling. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Approaching others by moving their hearts, and staying upright, brings good fortune. Influence people through genuine sincerity."],
    ["Approaching through mutual feeling. Good fortune. Nothing that does not further.", "Approaching others by moving their hearts brings good fortune, and everything goes well. Those above and below are of one mind, and the situation is excellent."],
    ["Approaching with sweetness. Nothing that would further. Once one grieves over it, no blame.", "Approaching people with sweet talk brings no benefit. But if you become uneasy about it and change your ways, there is no blame."],
    ["Approaching in person. No blame.", "Showing up in person brings no blame. Lead by example and do the work yourself."],
    ["Approaching with wisdom, as befits a great ruler. Good fortune.", "Governing with wisdom is what a true ruler should do, and it brings good fortune. Know people well and put them in the right roles."],
    ["Approaching with generous sincerity. Good fortune. No blame.", "Approaching others with generosity and warmth brings good fortune and no blame. Treat people kindly and good results will follow in the end."]
  ],
  20: [
    ["Viewing like a child. For the petty person, no blame; for the superior person, humiliation.", "Viewing things with a child's shallow eyes is no fault for the petty person, but a cause for regret for the superior person. Take the longer view."],
    ["Viewing through a chink in the door. It furthers a woman to persevere.", "Peeking through a crack in the door suits a woman who keeps to her proper place. Your view is narrow, so it is best to stick to your own role."],
    ["Viewing one's own life to decide advance or retreat.", "Look at your own conduct to decide whether to go forward or pull back. Reflect on yourself first, then set your course."],
    ["Viewing the glory of the kingdom. It furthers one to be received as the king's guest.", "Seeing the glory of the kingdom, it is fitting to come before the king as an honored guest. You have a chance to put your talents to use — seize it."],
    ["Viewing one's own life. For the superior person, no blame.", "By examining his own conduct, the superior person remains without blame. Those in high positions should reflect on themselves constantly."],
    ["Viewing the lives of others. For the superior person, no blame.", "By observing how others live, the superior person remains without blame. Even after stepping back, keep up the habit of self-examination."]
  ],
  21: [
    ["Feet in the stocks, the toes hidden. No blame.", "Feet locked in the stocks, toes hidden from view — no blame. A small punishment serves as a big warning; stop early."],
    ["Biting into soft flesh until the nose is buried. No blame.", "Biting into soft meat so deeply the nose sinks in — no blame. When handling easy matters, going a little too far does no harm."],
    ["Biting into dried meat and meeting poison. Slight humiliation. No blame.", "Biting into tough dried meat, you hit something poisonous — a small regret, but no blame. Stubborn resistance causes minor trouble, not a serious mistake."],
    ["Biting into dried meat on the bone, one gains a metal arrow. It furthers one to persevere in hardship. Good fortune.", "Biting through dried meat on the bone, you gain a character as straight and firm as a metal arrow. Stay upright through hardship and good fortune follows."],
    ["Biting into dried meat, one gains yellow gold. Perseverance, with danger. No blame.", "Biting through dried meat, you find yellow gold — the firmness of the middle way. Stay upright but remain cautious, and there is no blame."],
    ["Wearing the cangue, the ears hidden. Misfortune.", "Carrying a cangue that covers the ears — misfortune. Wrongdoing that is never corrected ends in disaster."]
  ],
  22: [
    ["Adorning his feet, he leaves the carriage and walks.", "He adorns his feet, gives up the carriage and goes on foot. Be content with your station and don't chase vanity."],
    ["Adorning the beard.", "Grooming the beard. It moves only with the face it belongs to — adornment is merely an accompaniment to something else."],
    ["Adorned and glistening. Lasting perseverance brings good fortune.", "Adorned, glossy and radiant — lasting steadfastness brings good fortune. Amid beauty, don't lose sight of substance."],
    ["Adorned, yet plain white; a white horse comes as if flying. Not a raider, but a suitor.", "Plain white adornment; a white horse gallops up. The rider is no bandit but a suitor. A return to simplicity — good news is near."],
    ["Adornment in the hill garden. The bolt of silk is meager. Humiliation, but in the end good fortune.", "Adorning the hills and gardens, offering only a thin roll of silk as a gift. It may look shabby, but it ends in good fortune. Value simplicity and thrift."],
    ["Plain white adornment. No blame.", "Adornment of plain white — no blame. The highest beauty is unadorned simplicity."]
  ],
  23: [
    ["Stripping the bed at its legs. Perseverance is scorned. Misfortune.", "The legs of the bed are being eaten away and the right way is scorned — misfortune. The crisis begins at the foundation."],
    ["Stripping the bed at its frame. Perseverance is scorned. Misfortune.", "The frame of the bed is being eaten away and the right way is scorned — misfortune. The crisis is drawing close."],
    ["Amid the stripping, no blame.", "In the midst of the stripping away, yet without blame. Keep your distance from the crowd of petty people and keep your heart set on the right way."],
    ["Stripping the bed down to the skin. Misfortune.", "The stripping has reached the skin of the person on the bed — misfortune. The disaster now touches you directly."],
    ["Fish strung on a line; favor as for the palace ladies. Nothing that does not further.", "Leading the others like fish strung on a line, winning favor as the palace ladies do with their lord — everything goes well. Leading by the right way turns danger into safety."],
    ["A great fruit left uneaten. The superior person gains a carriage; the petty person's hut is stripped away.", "The great fruit is left uneaten. The superior person gains a carriage — the support of the people — while the petty person loses even his roof. When stripping away reaches its limit, renewal follows; the right way endures."]
  ],
  24: [
    ["Returning before going far. No great remorse. Supreme good fortune.", "Turning back before going far, with no great regret — supreme good fortune. Correct your mistakes early."],
    ["A graceful return. Good fortune.", "A graceful return to the right path brings good fortune. When you see someone worthy, strive to match them."],
    ["Returning again and again. Danger. No blame.", "Straying again and again, and turning back again and again — there is danger, but no blame. What matters is that you can change."],
    ["Walking in the midst of others, he alone returns.", "Amid the crowd, you alone return to the right way. Hold to your principles and don't drift with the current."],
    ["A sincere and steadfast return. No remorse.", "Returning with sincerity and depth brings no regret. Reflect on yourself honestly."],
    ["Losing the way back. Misfortune; calamity and disaster. If armies are sent out, there will be a great defeat in the end, and misfortune for the ruler of the state. For ten years no campaign can succeed.", "Lost and failing to turn back — misfortune and calamity. If troops are sent out, they will suffer a great defeat, bringing disaster even to the ruler, and for ten years no campaign will be possible. Persisting in error leads to endless trouble."]
  ],
  25: [
    ["Without falsehood. Going forward brings good fortune.", "Acting without falsehood or recklessness, going forward brings good fortune. Follow your true heart."],
    ["Not plowing, yet reaping; not clearing, yet having a ripe field? Then it furthers one to have somewhere to go.", "Hoping to reap without sowing, or to have a ripe field without clearing it? Only by not seeking what you haven't earned and doing honest work will going forward pay off."],
    ["Misfortune without fault. Someone tethers an ox; the traveler's gain is the townsman's loss.", "Unexpected misfortune: someone tethers an ox by the road, a passerby leads it away, and the people of the town fall under suspicion. Trouble you did nothing to cause — face it with equanimity."],
    ["One can persevere. No blame.", "You can hold to what is right, and there is no blame. Simply keep to your own role."],
    ["An illness not of one's own making. Without medicine there is joy.", "An illness you did not bring on yourself will clear up without medicine. Don't interfere too much; wait for things to heal on their own."],
    ["Without falsehood, yet action brings calamity. Nothing that would further.", "Even without acting falsely, moving now brings trouble, and nothing is gained. The timing is wrong — stay still rather than act."]
  ],
  26: [
    ["There is danger. It furthers one to stop.", "Danger lies ahead, so it is best to stop. Knowing when to halt is how you build up strength."],
    ["The axle block comes off the cart.", "The axle comes loose from the cart, and it stops of its own accord. Stop within your limits and don't rush ahead."],
    ["Good horses in pursuit. It furthers one to persevere in hardship. Drill daily with chariot and guard. It furthers one to have somewhere to go.", "Fine horses race in pursuit; it pays to stay upright amid hardship. Train daily with chariot and defense, and going forward will go well. Prepare thoroughly before you set out."],
    ["A crossboard on the young bull's horns. Supreme good fortune.", "Fixing a crossboard to a young bull's horns so it cannot gore — supreme good fortune. Prevent trouble before it starts."],
    ["The tusks of a gelded boar. Good fortune.", "A gelded boar still has its tusks but does no harm — good fortune. Defuse problems at the root rather than meeting them head-on."],
    ["How open is the highway of heaven! Success.", "Moving freely along heaven's open highway — success. Your reserves are full, and the road ahead is boundless."]
  ],
  27: [
    ["You set aside your sacred tortoise and watch my working jaws. Misfortune.", "You set aside your own sacred tortoise — your own wisdom and resources — and stare instead at another's working jaws. Misfortune. Not standing on your own, you covet what others have."],
    ["Turning upside down for nourishment, departing from the norm; seeking nourishment from the hill. Going on brings misfortune.", "Turning downward for support goes against the natural order, and seeking it from the high hill means misfortune if you press on. When you ask for help, ask the right people."],
    ["Going against nourishment. Perseverance brings misfortune. Do not act so for ten years. Nothing that would further.", "Going against the proper way of nourishment and persisting in it brings misfortune. Don't act this way for ten years; nothing is gained."],
    ["Turning upside down for nourishment. Good fortune. The tiger gazes intently, its desire unrelenting. No blame.", "Turning downward for support brings good fortune. Like a tiger with a fixed, intent gaze, eagerly seeking worthy people — no blame."],
    ["Departing from the norm. Abiding in perseverance brings good fortune. One should not cross the great water.", "Departing from the usual way by relying on others, yet staying put and upright brings good fortune. Don't take risks by crossing the great river."],
    ["The source of nourishment. Danger, then good fortune. It furthers one to cross the great water.", "Everyone depends on him for nourishment. There is danger but also good fortune, and it is favorable to cross the great river. Take on great responsibility, and proceed with care."]
  ],
  28: [
    ["A mat of white rushes beneath. No blame.", "Laying clean white rushes underneath — no blame. Be doubly careful in what you do."],
    ["A withered willow puts out shoots; an old man gains a young wife. Nothing that does not further.", "A withered willow puts out new shoots; an old man takes a young wife. Everything goes well. An old tree meets spring and comes back to life."],
    ["The ridgepole sags. Misfortune.", "The ridgepole bends — misfortune. Stubborn and self-willed, you cannot bear the weight."],
    ["The ridgepole is raised. Good fortune. If there is another concern, humiliation.", "The ridgepole holds firm — good fortune. But if your attention is divided, there will be regret. Only with single-minded focus can you carry the load."],
    ["A withered willow puts out blossoms; an old woman gains a young husband. No blame, no praise.", "A withered willow blossoms; an old woman marries a young man. No blame, but no praise either. The flourishing is only on the surface and won't last."],
    ["Wading across, the water closes over the head. Misfortune. No blame.", "Wading too deep, the water closes over your head — misfortune, but the fault is not yours. Braving danger for a just cause brings misfortune without blame."]
  ],
  29: [
    ["Pit upon pit; one enters the depths of the pit. Misfortune.", "Peril upon peril, falling deep into the bottom of the pit — misfortune. One mistake follows another and you sink deeper."],
    ["In the pit there is danger. Seek small gains.", "There is danger in the pit, so aim only for small gains. Seek small successes first and steady your footing."],
    ["Coming and going, pit upon pit, perilous and deep; one enters the depths of the pit. Do not act.", "Pits whichever way you turn, dangerous and deep; you have fallen into the depths. Do not make any rash move."],
    ["A cup of wine, two bowls of grain, in earthen vessels; the pledge passed in through the window. In the end, no blame.", "A jug of wine and two bowls of rice in plain earthenware, passed simply through the window — in the end, no blame. In times of danger, deal with others sincerely and keep things simple."],
    ["The pit is not full; it is nearly level. No blame.", "The pit is not yet full, but it is nearly level. No blame. The danger is about to pass — don't rush ahead."],
    ["Bound with cords, set among thorn bushes; for three years one finds no way out. Misfortune.", "Tied with ropes and confined among thorns, for three years there is no release — misfortune. Deeply trapped, you can only endure for the long haul."]
  ],
  30: [
    ["Footsteps crisscross. Treat it with reverence. No blame.", "Your steps are confused and crossing; meet this with reverence and there is no blame. Stay respectful and careful as you set out."],
    ["Yellow radiance. Supreme good fortune.", "Yellow light — supreme good fortune. Keeping to the center and to what is right, your light shines on all."],
    ["Radiance of the declining sun. If one does not beat the pot and sing, there will be the laments of old age. Misfortune.", "In the light of the setting sun, if you don't beat the pot and sing, you will lament old age — misfortune. Face rise and decline with an open heart."],
    ["Suddenly it comes, it blazes, it dies, it is cast away.", "It arrives suddenly, blazes like fire, then dies and is cast aside. What comes on with violent force never lasts."],
    ["Tears pour down; grieving and sighing. Good fortune.", "Tears streaming down, sighing in sorrow — good fortune. Anxious self-reflection is what keeps you safe."],
    ["The king sends him forth to campaign. It is praiseworthy to strike off the head, taking captive not the followers. No blame.", "The king goes to war and rewards those who strike down the chief offender, capturing only the ringleaders and sparing the followers — no blame. Root out evil at its source and be lenient with the rank and file."]
  ],
  31: [
    ["Stirring in the big toe.", "The stirring is felt in the big toe. Intentions are just beginning to stir and haven't yet turned into action."],
    ["Stirring in the calves. Misfortune. Staying put brings good fortune.", "The stirring is felt in the calves. Acting rashly brings misfortune; staying put brings good fortune. Don't follow impulses blindly."],
    ["Stirring in the thighs; holding to what it follows. Going on brings humiliation.", "The stirring is felt in the thighs, and you insist on following others; going on brings regret. Don't just drift with the crowd."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. Remorse vanishes. Coming and going restlessly, only friends follow your thoughts.", "Staying upright brings good fortune and regret disappears. If your thoughts keep wavering back and forth, only those of your own kind will go along with you. Moving others with an upright heart beats deliberate maneuvering."],
    ["Stirring in the back. No remorse.", "The stirring is felt in the back — no regret. Your heart is not swayed by outside things."],
    ["Stirring in the jaws, cheeks and tongue.", "The stirring is felt in the jaws, cheeks and tongue. Trying to move people with words alone is showy but empty."]
  ],
  32: [
    ["Digging deep for constancy. Perseverance brings misfortune. Nothing that would further.", "Demanding permanence too deeply right at the start — persisting in this brings misfortune, and nothing is gained. Rushing for results means they won't last."],
    ["Remorse vanishes.", "Regret disappears. By keeping to the middle way, you persevere steadily."],
    ["Not constant in virtue, one may meet disgrace. Perseverance brings humiliation.", "If you cannot keep your virtue constant, disgrace is hard to avoid, and persisting brings regret. Being changeable loses you people's trust."],
    ["No game in the field.", "Hunting in the field, but there is no game. If the direction is wrong, persistence is wasted effort."],
    ["Constant in virtue, persevering: good fortune for a wife, misfortune for a husband.", "Keeping virtue constant and staying upright is good fortune for a wife but misfortune for a man. It depends on the person and the situation — don't simply go along with others."],
    ["Constancy shaken. Misfortune.", "Seeking constancy in a restless, unsettled way brings misfortune. Agitated persistence cannot last."]
  ],
  33: [
    ["Retreating at the tail. Danger. Do not undertake anything.", "You are last to retreat, which is dangerous; it is not the time to act. You left it too late, so stay still and wait."],
    ["He holds him fast with yellow oxhide. No one can tear him loose.", "Bound tight with yellow oxhide, no one can break free. Your will is firm and nothing moves you."],
    ["A retreat held back by ties. Illness and danger. To keep servants and maids brings good fortune.", "Your heart is tied down and you cannot withdraw, which brings illness and danger; looking after servants brings good fortune. If you cannot let go, handle only small matters."],
    ["Retreat in spite of what one loves. For the superior person, good fortune; for the petty person, not so.", "You withdraw even though there is something you are fond of. The superior person meets good fortune; the petty person cannot do this. Let go of private attachments and retreat when it is time."],
    ["Admirable retreat. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Withdrawing gracefully and at the right moment; staying upright brings good fortune. A well-timed, elegant exit."],
    ["Cheerful retreat. Everything furthers.", "Withdrawing at ease, nothing fails to benefit you. With nothing weighing on your mind, the sky is wide open."]
  ],
  34: [
    ["Strength in the toes. Advancing brings misfortune — this is certain.", "Strength sits only in the toes, so pushing forward brings misfortune; that much is certain. Your power is just beginning, so do not rush ahead."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Staying upright brings good fortune. Balance firmness with gentleness and do not lean on your strength."],
    ["The petty person uses strength; the superior person does not. Perseverance brings danger. A ram butts against a hedge and gets its horns entangled.", "The petty person shows off his strength, while the superior person does not use brute force; persisting in force is dangerous. The ram that charges the fence only gets its horns stuck."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. Remorse vanishes. The hedge opens; there is no entanglement. Strength lies in the axle of a great cart.", "Staying upright brings good fortune and remorse vanishes. The fence gives way and the horns are not caught; strength rests in the axle of a great cart, where it can truly be used."],
    ["He loses the ram with ease. No remorse.", "The ram is lost easily at the field's edge, without regret. Set aside hardness and let gentleness overcome strength."],
    ["A ram butts against a hedge. It cannot go back, it cannot go forward. Nothing furthers. Through hardship, good fortune.", "The ram charges the fence and can neither retreat nor advance; nothing is gained. Reflecting in hardship brings good fortune. Forcing things to the end only leaves you stuck either way."]
  ],
  35: [
    ["Advancing, yet held back. Perseverance brings good fortune. If not yet trusted, stay generous. No blame.", "You meet resistance as you advance; staying upright brings good fortune. If you have not yet won people's trust, wait with an easy, generous heart and there is no blame."],
    ["Advancing, but in sorrow. Perseverance brings good fortune. One receives great blessing from one's grandmother.", "You advance with a worried heart, but staying upright brings good fortune; great blessing will come from a grandmother or an elder."],
    ["All are in accord. Remorse vanishes.", "You win everyone's trust and remorse vanishes. With the people behind you, your advance stands on solid ground."],
    ["Advancing like a hamster. Perseverance brings danger.", "Advancing like a greedy, incapable rodent; persisting this way is dangerous. Your virtue does not match your position."],
    ["Remorse vanishes. Do not fret over loss or gain. Going forward brings good fortune. Everything furthers.", "Remorse vanishes; do not worry over gains and losses. Going forward brings good fortune and everything benefits you. Let go of the fear of winning and losing."],
    ["Advancing with the horns. Use them only to discipline one's own city. Danger, then good fortune. No blame. Perseverance brings humiliation.", "You have advanced to the tip of the horns and can only use your force to put your own city in order. There is danger, yet good fortune and no blame, but holding on unchanged brings regret. Look inward rather than expanding outward."]
  ],
  36: [
    ["Darkening of the light in flight; he lowers his wings. The superior person on his way goes three days without eating. Wherever he goes, the host has words for him.", "The light is wounded, like a bird lowering its wings in flight. The superior person travels three days without eating, and wherever he goes the host criticizes him. Hide your edge and get away quickly."],
    ["Darkening of the light; he is wounded in the left thigh. He gives aid with the strength of a horse. Good fortune.", "The light is wounded and the left thigh injured; rescue comes with the help of a strong horse, which brings good fortune. When you suffer a setback, seek powerful support."],
    ["Darkening of the light during the hunt in the south. Their great leader is captured. One must not hurry to set things right.", "The light is wounded while hunting in the south, yet the chief wrongdoer is captured; still, do not act in haste. Clear away what is wrong step by step."],
    ["He enters the left side of the belly. He grasps the heart of the darkening of the light, and leaves gate and courtyard.", "Going deep into the left side of the belly, you learn the inner truth of the darkness, and so you walk out the gate and leave. Once you see things as they are, leave decisively."],
    ["Darkening of the light, as with Jizi. Perseverance furthers.", "Like Jizi, hide your light in the midst of darkness and stay upright. Appear foolish outside while remaining clear within, and keep to the right path."],
    ["Not light but darkness. First he climbed up to heaven; then he plunged into the earth.", "No light, only darkness. At first he rose to the heights of heaven, but in the end he fell into the earth. Whoever loses the way will bring about his own ruin."]
  ],
  37: [
    ["Firm rules within the family. Remorse vanishes.", "Set rules when the household is first formed and remorse vanishes. Establish the family's ways first."],
    ["She does not follow her own whims. She tends to the food within. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Not acting on one's own whims but devoting oneself to the household's meals; staying upright brings good fortune. Each keeps to their own role."],
    ["When the household is strict, there is remorse and danger, yet good fortune. When women and children laugh and trifle, humiliation in the end.", "A strict household may bring remorse and danger, but it ends in good fortune; if women and children frolic without restraint, there will be regret in the end. In running a home, better too strict than too lax."],
    ["She enriches the household. Supreme good fortune.", "Making the household prosperous brings supreme good fortune. Good management makes the family flourish."],
    ["The king approaches his family. Have no fear. Good fortune.", "The king wins over his family through virtue; there is no need to worry, and good fortune follows. Lead by example, and a harmonious home makes everything prosper."],
    ["With sincerity and dignity, good fortune in the end.", "Being both sincere and dignified brings good fortune in the end. Hold the family together with honesty and authority."]
  ],
  38: [
    ["Remorse vanishes. If you lose your horse, do not chase it; it will return by itself. Seeing evil people — no blame.", "Remorse vanishes. If you lose your horse, do not chase it; it will come back on its own. Even meeting bad people brings no blame. Dissolve the distance with tolerance."],
    ["He meets his lord in a narrow lane. No blame.", "You meet your lord in a narrow lane, and there is no blame. Differences are resolved in an informal setting."],
    ["One sees the wagon dragged back, the oxen halted, the man's hair and nose cut off. No good beginning, but a good end.", "You see the cart held back and the oxen pulled up short, and the driver has suffered the branding and nose-cutting punishments. Things go badly at first but turn out well in the end."],
    ["Isolated through estrangement, one meets a like-minded person and they associate in sincerity. Danger, but no blame.", "Isolated and estranged, you meet a good person who shares your aims; dealing with each other sincerely, there is danger but no blame."],
    ["Remorse vanishes. The kinsman bites through the soft flesh. If one goes forward, how could it be a mistake?", "Remorse vanishes. Your kinsfolk come together as easily as biting into tender meat; what fault could there be in going forward?"],
    ["Isolated through estrangement, one sees a pig covered with mud and a cart full of ghosts. First he draws his bow, then he lays it aside. He is not a robber; he will woo at the right time. Going forward, one meets rain; then good fortune.", "Isolated and estranged, suspicion breeds phantoms: you see a pig caked in mud and a cart full of ghosts. You draw your bow to shoot, then lower it; he is not a robber but a suitor. Going forward and meeting rain brings good fortune; once doubts are gone, you can make peace."]
  ],
  39: [
    ["Going leads to obstruction; coming back brings praise.", "Going forward meets danger, while coming back wins praise. Stop when you see danger."],
    ["The king's servant is beset by obstruction upon obstruction, but it is not his own fault.", "The king's servant goes through hardship after hardship, and not for his own sake. Working for the common good, there is no regret despite the difficulty."],
    ["Going leads to obstruction; so he comes back.", "Going forward meets danger, and coming back lets you settle securely. Return to your proper place."],
    ["Going leads to obstruction; coming back brings union.", "Going forward meets danger, while coming back lets you join with others. Gather your strength together before trying to advance again."],
    ["In the midst of the greatest obstruction, friends come.", "In great difficulty, friends come to help. Hardship reveals true friendship."],
    ["Going leads to obstruction; coming back leads to great things. Good fortune. It furthers one to see the great man.", "Going forward meets danger, while coming back lets you achieve great things; good fortune, and it is wise to visit a person of virtue and standing. Seek out the wise to resolve your difficulty."]
  ],
  40: [
    ["No blame.", "No blame. The difficulty has just been lifted; simply rest and recover."],
    ["In the field he catches three foxes and obtains a yellow arrow. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "On the hunt you catch three foxes and gain a yellow arrow; staying upright brings good fortune. Remove the cunning and the crooked, and hold to the balanced center."],
    ["Carrying a burden on his back, yet riding in a carriage, he invites robbers. Perseverance brings humiliation.", "Carrying goods on your back while riding in a carriage invites robbers; persisting this way brings regret. When virtue does not match position, others start to covet what you have."],
    ["Free yourself from your big toe. Then friends come, and with them sincerity.", "Free your big toe — shake off the clinging of petty people — and only then will friends deal with you sincerely."],
    ["If the superior person can deliver himself, good fortune. This proves his sincerity to the petty person.", "The superior person is able to resolve the difficulty, which brings good fortune, and even the petty people are won over. Win people through virtue."],
    ["The prince shoots at a hawk on a high wall. He kills it. Everything furthers.", "A noble shoots a hawk from atop a high wall and hits it with one shot; everything benefits. When the time is ripe, remove the harm in a single stroke."]
  ],
  41: [
    ["When one's own affairs are done, go quickly. No blame. But consider how much one may decrease.", "Once your own work is done, hurry to help others, and there is no blame; but weigh carefully how much of yourself to give."],
    ["Perseverance furthers. Undertaking brings misfortune. Without decreasing oneself, one can increase others.", "It is wise to stay upright; rushing ahead brings misfortune. Without diminishing yourself, you can add to others."],
    ["When three people travel together, one is lost. When one travels alone, he finds a companion.", "Three traveling together will lose one; one traveling alone will find a friend. In relationships, single-minded commitment is what counts."],
    ["If one lessens one's faults, it brings swift joy. No blame.", "Reduce your own faults so that joy comes quickly; there is no blame. Correct your shortcomings early."],
    ["Someone increases him with a tortoise worth ten strings of shells; it cannot be refused. Supreme good fortune.", "Someone presents a great tortoise worth ten strings of shells and you cannot refuse it; supreme good fortune. Blessings arrive unsought, as if from heaven."],
    ["Without decreasing, he increases others. No blame. Perseverance brings good fortune. It furthers one to undertake something. He wins servants, no longer bound to one household.", "Adding to others without diminishing yourself brings no blame; staying upright brings good fortune and it is good to set out. You win people's hearts far beyond a single household."]
  ],
  42: [
    ["It furthers one to accomplish great deeds. Supreme good fortune. No blame.", "It is a good time to achieve something great; supreme good fortune and no blame. Seize the chance to do big things."],
    ["Someone increases him with a tortoise worth ten strings of shells; it cannot be refused. Constant perseverance brings good fortune. The king presents him before God. Good fortune.", "Someone presents a great tortoise worth ten strings of shells and you cannot refuse it; long-lasting uprightness brings good fortune. The king offers it in sacrifice to the Lord on High, and there is good fortune."],
    ["One is enriched through unfortunate events. No blame. With sincerity, walking in the middle, one reports to the prince with a jade tablet.", "You gain something even through misfortune, and there is no blame; with sincerity and keeping to the middle way, you report to the prince holding a jade tablet. Danger holds opportunity; speak honestly."],
    ["Walking in the middle, he reports to the prince, who follows. It furthers one to be relied upon in moving the capital.", "Keeping to the middle way, you advise the prince and are heeded; it is fitting to support the larger plan of moving the capital. In great upheaval, serve as the bridge."],
    ["With sincerity and a kind heart, do not ask. Supreme good fortune. Sincerity will be returned as kindness to one's virtue.", "Show kindness with a sincere heart, with no need to ask; supreme good fortune. People in turn will sincerely remember your virtue."],
    ["He brings increase to no one; someone even strikes him. He does not keep his heart constant. Misfortune.", "No one adds to him, and someone even attacks him; his resolve does not last, and there is misfortune. Those who seek only their own gain are eventually abandoned by all."]
  ],
  43: [
    ["Strength in the advancing toes. Going, he does not prevail, and this is a mistake.", "Charging ahead on the strength of your toes alone, you will not win, and you will be at fault. You are not prepared enough, so do not rush."],
    ["Alert and crying out. Even if armed men come at nightfall, do not fear.", "Stay alert and call out; even if enemies come in the night there is no need to worry. Preparation prevents disaster."],
    ["Strength in the cheekbones brings misfortune. The superior person is firmly resolved. Walking alone, he meets rain and gets wet. People are angry with him, but no blame.", "Showing anger on your face brings misfortune. The superior person decides resolutely; walking alone, he is caught in the rain and soaked, and though others resent him, in the end there is no blame."],
    ["There is no skin on his buttocks, and walking is hard. If he let himself be led like a sheep, remorse would vanish. But if he hears these words, he will not believe them.", "With no flesh on the buttocks, you hobble forward haltingly. If you let yourself be led along like a sheep, remorse would vanish — but you probably will not believe it when told."],
    ["Weeds are uprooted with firm resolve. Walking in the middle — no blame.", "Clear things away as decisively as pulling up purslane; keeping to the middle way, there is no blame."],
    ["No cry for help. In the end, misfortune.", "There is no one left to cry out to, and misfortune comes in the end. The petty person has reached a dead end beyond saving."]
  ],
  44: [
    ["It must be checked with a brake of bronze. Perseverance brings good fortune. If one lets it run, misfortune appears. Even a lean pig is restless and stamping.", "Hold it fast with a metal brake, and staying upright brings good fortune; if you let it run, you will meet misfortune, restless as a lean pig. Stop it early."],
    ["There is a fish in the tank. No blame. It does not further guests.", "There is fish in the kitchen; no blame, but do not hand it to outsiders. Keep the problem within your own control."],
    ["There is no skin on his buttocks, and walking is hard. Danger, but no great mistake.", "With no flesh on the buttocks, you hobble forward haltingly. There is danger, but no great blame."],
    ["No fish in the tank. Rising brings misfortune.", "There is no fish in the kitchen; making a move brings misfortune. You have lost the people's support and your foundation."],
    ["A melon wrapped in leaves of the qi tree. Hidden beauty. Then it falls down from heaven.", "Melons wrapped in the leaves of the qi tree: carry your virtues within rather than on display, and in time an opportunity will fall from heaven."],
    ["He meets with horns. Humiliation. No blame.", "Meeting at the tip of the horns brings regret, but no blame. Aloof and holding to yourself, you find it hard to get along with others."]
  ],
  45: [
    ["Sincere, but not to the end; so there is confusion and gathering. If one cries out, then after one clasp of hands there is laughter. Do not worry. Going forward — no blame.", "You are sincere but cannot keep it up, so your mind is in turmoil and you gather with others haphazardly. If you call out, tears turn to laughter with a single handshake. Do not worry; going forward brings no blame."],
    ["Being drawn in brings good fortune. No blame. If one is sincere, even a small offering is fitting.", "Being drawn into the gathering brings good fortune and no blame; with sincerity, even a modest offering reaches the spirits. A sincere heart matters more than display."],
    ["Gathering together amid sighs. Nothing furthers. Going forward — no blame. Slight humiliation.", "You want to join in but can only sigh, and nothing is gained; going forward brings no blame, though with a little regret. Taking the first step may be a bit awkward, but it still works."],
    ["Supreme good fortune. No blame.", "Only supreme good fortune brings freedom from blame. Your position is not quite right, so you must do things flawlessly to avoid fault."],
    ["Gathering with a position of honor. No blame. If some are not yet trusting, sublime and lasting perseverance makes remorse vanish.", "You hold a high position in the gathering, and there is no blame; if you have not yet won people's trust, stay upright from start to finish and remorse will vanish."],
    ["Lamenting and sighing, flowing tears. No blame.", "Sighing and weeping with tears streaming down, there is no blame. Through worry and self-reflection, you can keep yourself safe in the end."]
  ],
  46: [
    ["Rising that meets with trust. Supreme good fortune.", "Rising because you are trusted brings supreme good fortune. You have the backing of those above you."],
    ["If one is sincere, even a small offering is fitting. No blame.", "With sincerity, even a modest offering reaches the spirits; no blame. Advance through sincerity."],
    ["He rises into an empty city.", "You rise into an empty city and move forward without obstruction."],
    ["The king makes offering on Mount Qi. Good fortune. No blame.", "The king offers sacrifice on Mount Qi; good fortune and no blame. Go with the flow of events and you will be given important responsibilities."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. One rises step by step.", "Staying upright brings good fortune as you climb the steps one by one. Advance gradually and rise steadily."],
    ["Rising in darkness. It furthers one to be unremittingly persevering.", "Rising blindly and without pause, it is wise to stay upright without ceasing. You know only how to go up and not when to stop, so you need the right path to keep yourself in check."]
  ],
  47: [
    ["One sits oppressed under a bare tree stump and strays into a gloomy valley. For three years one sees nothing.", "Sitting stuck on a tree stump, you enter a dark valley and see no daylight for three years. In hard times, be patient."],
    ["Oppressed while at meat and drink. The man with the scarlet sash is just coming. It furthers one to offer sacrifice. Setting forth brings misfortune. No blame.", "You are troubled over food and drink — material life is not going smoothly — but the scarlet robes of office are about to arrive. It is fitting to make sincere offerings; rushing ahead brings misfortune, yet there is no blame."],
    ["Oppressed by stone, leaning on thorns and thistles. He enters his house and does not see his wife. Misfortune.", "Trapped under a rock and leaning on thorns, you return home and your wife is not there; misfortune. You have nowhere to stand, forward or back."],
    ["He comes very slowly, oppressed in a golden carriage. Humiliation, but the end is reached.", "You arrive slowly, held up in a golden carriage — held back by others. There is regret, but it comes to an outcome in the end."],
    ["His nose and feet are cut off. Oppressed by the man with the red sash. Joy comes slowly. It furthers one to make offerings and sacrifices.", "Suffering the punishment of having nose and feet cut off, you are oppressed by the powerful, but you can free yourself little by little; it is fitting to make sincere offerings."],
    ["He is oppressed by creeping vines. He moves unsteadily and says, 'Movement brings remorse.' If one feels remorse over this, setting forth brings good fortune.", "Tangled in creeping vines, you stand in a shaky, perilous place. If you say 'every move I make brings regret' and truly come to repent, going forward brings good fortune."]
  ],
  48: [
    ["One does not drink the mud of the well. No animals come to an old well.", "The mud at the bottom of the well cannot be drunk, and not even birds visit an abandoned old well. If you do not cultivate yourself, no one pays you any attention."],
    ["At the wellhole one shoots fishes. The jug is broken and leaks.", "The water in the well is only enough to shoot at little fish, and the drawing jar is cracked and leaking. Your talents have no place to be used."],
    ["The well is cleaned, but no one drinks from it. This is my heart's sorrow, for one might draw from it. If the king were clear-minded, all would share in the blessing.", "The well has been cleaned, yet no one comes to drink, and it pains the heart. If a clear-sighted king put it to use, everyone would share the blessing. Talent goes unrecognized while it waits to be appreciated."],
    ["The well is being lined. No blame.", "The well's walls are being lined with brick; no blame. Cultivate yourself first, then seek to serve the world."],
    ["In the well there is a clear, cold spring from which one can drink.", "The well water is clear and the spring is cool, fit for people to drink. With both virtue and talent, your benefit reaches everyone."],
    ["One draws from the well without covering it. With sincerity, supreme good fortune.", "The well is drawn from and left uncovered; with sincerity, supreme good fortune. Share the fruits with others."]
  ],
  49: [
    ["Bound fast with the hide of a yellow ox.", "Bound tightly with yellow oxhide. The time for change has not yet come; hold firm."],
    ["On the day of completion, carry out the change. Going forth brings good fortune. No blame.", "Make the change only when the proper day arrives; going forward brings good fortune, no blame. Act once the time is ripe."],
    ["Going forth brings misfortune. Perseverance brings danger. When talk of change has gone round three times, one gains sincerity.", "Rushing ahead brings misfortune, yet standing still is also dangerous. Only after a proposal for change has been discussed again and again will people trust it."],
    ["Remorse vanishes. With sincerity, changing the mandate brings good fortune.", "Remorse vanishes; changing the mandate with sincerity in your heart brings good fortune. The change has earned people's trust."],
    ["The great man changes like a tiger. Even before he consults the oracle, he has sincerity.", "The great man transforms like a tiger, his stripes shining bright; he has people's trust without even consulting the oracle."],
    ["The superior person changes like a leopard. The petty person changes his face. Going forth brings misfortune. Remaining in perseverance brings good fortune.", "The superior person transforms like a leopard's spots, and even the petty person changes his outward face. Rushing ahead brings misfortune; settling down and staying upright brings good fortune. The change is complete; now consolidate it."]
  ],
  50: [
    ["The cauldron is upturned on its legs. It furthers one to empty out what is foul. One takes a concubine for the sake of her son. No blame.", "The cauldron is tipped over on its legs, which conveniently empties out what is foul; taking a concubine brings benefit through her son. No blame. Turn a disadvantage into an advantage."],
    ["The cauldron is full. My rival is ailing and cannot come near me. Good fortune.", "The cauldron holds solid contents; your rival is ailing and cannot come near you. Good fortune. Keep yourself well-provisioned and outside trouble cannot reach you."],
    ["The handles of the cauldron are altered; its movement is blocked. The fat of the pheasant is not eaten. When rain falls, remorse is spent. In the end, good fortune.", "The cauldron's handles have come off, so it cannot be moved, and the fine pheasant fat goes uneaten; when the rain comes, remorse fades and in the end there is good fortune. A temporary obstruction will eventually clear."],
    ["The legs of the cauldron break. The prince's meal is spilled, and his person is soiled. Misfortune.", "The cauldron's legs snap and the prince's fine meal spills everywhere. Misfortune. Taking on a heavy load with too little strength is bound to end in a mishap."],
    ["The cauldron has yellow handles and golden carrying rings. Perseverance furthers.", "The cauldron is fitted with yellow handles and golden carrying rings; it is right to stay upright. Holding the center with an open mind, you attract capable people to assist you."],
    ["The cauldron has rings of jade. Supreme good fortune. Nothing that does not further.", "The cauldron is fitted with jade carrying rings. Supreme good fortune; everything is favorable. Firmness and gentleness balance each other, and a great work is completed."]
  ],
  51: [
    ["Shock comes - oh, oh! Then laughing words - ha, ha! Good fortune.", "Thunder strikes and you are shaken and uneasy; afterward you talk and laugh at ease. Good fortune. Fear comes first, then calm."],
    ["Shock comes bringing danger. A hundred thousand times one loses one's treasures and climbs the nine hills. Do not pursue them; after seven days one gets them back.", "Thunder strikes with danger and you lose a great deal of wealth; climb to the ninefold heights and do not chase after it - in seven days what was lost will return of itself."],
    ["Shock comes and one is distraught. If shock spurs one to action, there is no calamity.", "Thunder leaves you shaken and unsettled; if that fear makes you act carefully, there will be no disaster."],
    ["Shock is mired in the mud.", "The thunder sinks into the mud. You cannot rouse yourself; it is time for self-reflection."],
    ["Shock goes and comes; danger. Yet nothing is lost, and there are matters to attend to.", "Thunder comes and goes, both dangerous; but if you keep a firm hold on your purpose, nothing will be lost and you can still get things done."],
    ["Shock brings trembling and frightened glances. Going forth brings misfortune. If the shock has not yet touched oneself but only one's neighbor, there is no blame. Marriage partners have words.", "Thunder leaves you trembling and looking about in panic; rushing ahead brings misfortune. If you take precautions when the thunder strikes your neighbor rather than yourself, there is no blame - though there will be gossip around matters of marriage."]
  ],
  52: [
    ["Keeping his toes still. No blame. Continued perseverance furthers.", "Keeping the toes still: no blame, and it is right to stay upright for the long term. Stopping before you even set out keeps you from making mistakes."],
    ["Keeping his calves still. He cannot rescue the one he follows. His heart is not glad.", "Keeping the calves still, yet unable to save the one you follow, you are unhappy at heart. You can hold yourself back but cannot hold others back."],
    ["Keeping his hips still, wrenching his spine. Danger; the heart smolders.", "Stopping at the waist tears the flesh along the spine, with danger burning like fire in the heart. Forcible suppression harms body and mind alike."],
    ["Keeping his trunk still. No blame.", "Keeping the body still: no blame. Keep your own conduct in check."],
    ["Keeping his jaws still. The words have order. Remorse vanishes.", "Keeping the jaws still, your words are orderly and remorse vanishes. Be careful in what you say."],
    ["Noblehearted keeping still. Good fortune.", "Stopping steadfastly and generously where one ought to stop: good fortune. Finishing what you started - knowing where to stop brings stability."]
  ],
  53: [
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the shore. The young son is in danger; there is talk. No blame.", "The wild goose gradually flies to the water's edge; a young person faces danger and criticism, yet there is no blame. The start is hard - proceed step by step."],
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the rock. Eating and drinking in peace and joy. Good fortune.", "The wild goose gradually reaches a boulder and eats and drinks contentedly. Good fortune. Gradually settling in, with no worries about food or clothing."],
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the plateau. The husband goes forth and does not return; the wife carries a child but does not give birth. Misfortune. It furthers one to fend off robbers.", "The wild goose gradually reaches the high ground. The husband goes off on campaign and never returns, and the wife conceives but cannot bring the child to term. Misfortune; it is right to defend against raiders. Rash advances damage the family's fortunes."],
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the tree. Perhaps it finds a flat branch. No blame.", "The wild goose gradually reaches a tree and may find a flat, straight branch to perch on. No blame. Make yourself at home wherever you land."],
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the summit. For three years the wife does not conceive. In the end nothing can prevail against it. Good fortune.", "The wild goose gradually reaches the hilltop; the wife does not conceive for three years, but in the end no one can stand in the way. Good fortune. Good things take time, but they come to pass in the end."],
    ["The wild goose gradually draws near the plateau. Its feathers can be used in the sacred dance. Good fortune.", "The wild goose gradually reaches the high ground, and its feathers can adorn ceremonial regalia. Good fortune. Having achieved success, step back and become a model for others."]
  ],
  54: [
    ["The marrying maiden goes as a secondary wife. The lame can walk. Going forth brings good fortune.", "A maiden is married off as a secondary wife accompanying her sister, like a lame person who can still walk; going forward brings good fortune. You can accomplish things even in a secondary position."],
    ["The one-eyed can see. The perseverance of a solitary person furthers.", "Though your eyes are weak you can still see; it is right to stay upright like a recluse. Even when things don't go your way, keep your integrity."],
    ["The marrying maiden goes with lofty expectations; she is sent back and goes as a secondary wife.", "She held herself too high when marrying, was sent back, and went again as a secondary wife. Misjudging your place leads to being humbled."],
    ["The marrying maiden draws out the allotted time. A late marriage comes in due course.", "The marriage is delayed past its time; marrying late means waiting for the right moment. Better to wait than to settle."],
    ["The sovereign Di Yi gave his younger sister in marriage. The sleeves of the princess were not as fine as those of the secondary wife. The moon that is nearly full brings good fortune.", "When Di Yi gave his sister in marriage, the principal wife's sleeves were less splendid than those of the bride who accompanied her; like a moon nearly but not yet full, this brings good fortune. Noble yet modest and plain."],
    ["The woman holds the basket, but there is no fruit in it. The man stabs the sheep, but no blood flows. Nothing that furthers.", "The woman holds a basket with no fruit in it, and the man slaughters a sheep but no blood appears. Nothing is favorable. All form and no substance."]
  ],
  55: [
    ["He meets his matching lord. Though they are together ten days, no blame. Going forth meets with esteem.", "You meet a well-matched master; even spending ten days together brings no blame, and going forward wins esteem. Work together with one mind."],
    ["The abundance is screened off, so that at midday one sees the Dipper. Going forth meets with suspicion and hostility. With sincerity, awakening others brings good fortune.", "Abundance is screened off, so that the Dipper can be seen at midday; going forward meets with suspicion, but if you enlighten others with sincerity, there is good fortune."],
    ["The abundance is curtained off, so that at midday one sees the small stars. He breaks his right arm. No blame.", "Abundance is hidden behind a curtain, so that small stars can be seen at midday, and you break your right arm. No blame. For now there is no place to use your strengths, but it is not your fault."],
    ["The abundance is screened off, so that at midday one sees the Dipper. He meets his lord, his equal. Good fortune.", "Abundance is screened off, so that the Dipper can be seen at midday, but you meet a master who is your equal. Good fortune. You find someone who truly understands you."],
    ["Talented people come forward. Blessing and praise. Good fortune.", "You attract talented people, bringing celebration and acclaim. Good fortune. Welcome capable people widely."],
    ["His house is abundant, but his household is screened off. He peers through the gate: it is still, with no one there. For three years he sees no one. Misfortune.", "The house is grand but the household is shut away; peering through the gate, all is silent and empty, and no one is seen for three years. Misfortune. Arrogance and self-isolation drive everyone away."]
  ],
  56: [
    ["The wanderer busies himself with trivial things. Thus he brings calamity on himself.", "On the road, being petty, calculating, and mean-spirited only invites disaster on yourself."],
    ["The wanderer comes to an inn, with his property about him, and wins a loyal young servant. Perseverance.", "On the road you reach an inn with your money on you and gain a faithful young servant; stay upright. Far from home, you find a place of security."],
    ["The wanderer's inn burns down. He loses his young servant. Perseverance brings danger.", "On the road your inn burns down and you lose your young servant; holding on like this is dangerous. Being headstrong away from home costs you the goodwill of others."],
    ["The wanderer finds a resting place and obtains his property and an axe. My heart is not glad.", "On the road you find temporary shelter and gain money and an axe, but your heart is not glad. You have gained something, but not your proper place."],
    ["He shoots a pheasant; one arrow is lost. In the end this brings praise and office.", "Shooting at a pheasant, you lose an arrow, but in the end this earns you praise and an appointment. A small loss brings a great success."],
    ["The bird's nest burns. The wanderer first laughs, then wails and weeps. He loses his ox through carelessness. Misfortune.", "The bird's nest is set on fire; the wanderer laughs at first and then weeps aloud, and carelessly loses his ox at the field's edge. Misfortune. Getting carried away with success, you end up losing what you depend on."]
  ],
  57: [
    ["Advancing and retreating. The perseverance of a warrior furthers.", "Wavering between advance and retreat, it is right to hold firm with a warrior's decisiveness. When you have been too compliant, it is time to show resolve."],
    ["Yielding beneath the bed. Priests and diviners are used in great number. Good fortune. No blame.", "Humbly bowing low beneath the bed and employing many priests and diviners to communicate: good fortune, no blame. Use sincerity to communicate with those above and below."],
    ["Repeated, reluctant yielding. Humiliation.", "Yielding reluctantly again and again brings regret. Constantly swallowing your pride to keep the peace is not a long-term solution."],
    ["Remorse vanishes. During the hunt, three kinds of game are caught.", "Remorse vanishes, and the hunt yields three kinds of game. Going with the flow brings a rich harvest."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. Remorse vanishes. Nothing that does not further. No beginning, but an end. Three days before the change, three days after the change. Good fortune.", "Staying upright brings good fortune, remorse vanishes, and everything is favorable; things go badly at first but end well. Be careful for three days before and three days after a change. Good fortune."],
    ["Yielding beneath the bed. He loses his property and his axe. Perseverance brings misfortune.", "Humbly bowing low beneath the bed, you lose your money and your axe; holding on like this brings misfortune. Excessive submissiveness costs you the very ground you stand on."]
  ],
  58: [
    ["Harmonious joyousness. Good fortune.", "Treating others with warmth and good cheer brings good fortune. A calm, even temper keeps relationships harmonious."],
    ["Sincere joyousness. Good fortune. Remorse vanishes.", "Pleasing others through sincerity and trustworthiness brings good fortune, and remorse vanishes. Genuineness beats flattery."],
    ["Coming joyousness. Misfortune.", "Coming forward to curry favor brings misfortune. Deliberate fawning only invites humiliation."],
    ["Joyousness that is weighed is not at peace. After ridding himself of the affliction, he has joy.", "Weighing up whom to please leaves the mind unsettled; cut yourself off from the faults of petty people and there will be cause for celebration."],
    ["Sincerity toward disintegrating influences. There is danger.", "Trusting petty people who wear you down is dangerous. Keep away from flatterers."],
    ["Seductive joyousness.", "Luring others into shared pleasure-seeking. Sliding into indulgence calls for great caution."]
  ],
  59: [
    ["He brings help with the strength of a horse. Good fortune.", "Coming to the rescue with the help of a strong horse brings good fortune. As things begin to scatter, get help early to set them right."],
    ["At the dispersion he hurries to his support. Remorse vanishes.", "As things scatter, you hurry to something steady to lean on, and remorse vanishes. You find a place to settle."],
    ["He dissolves his self. No remorse.", "Letting go of the selfish ego brings no remorse. Set yourself aside and act for the common good."],
    ["He dissolves his bond with his group. Supreme good fortune. Dispersion leads to accumulation like a hill - something ordinary people do not think of.", "Disbanding private factions brings supreme good fortune; breaking up small cliques actually gathers people into a great body like a hill - something ordinary people would never think of."],
    ["Dispersing his great proclamation like sweat; dispersing the king's stores. No blame.", "Issuing a great proclamation, like sweat pouring out, and distributing the royal stores to help the people: no blame."],
    ["Dispersing the blood, he goes far away and out of danger. No blame.", "Keeping clear of bloodshed, going far away and escaping danger: no blame. Get away from harm in good time."]
  ],
  60: [
    ["Not going out of the door and the courtyard. No blame.", "Not leaving the inner courtyard of your home: no blame. Knowing the time has not yet come, you hold back and stay in."],
    ["Not going out of the gate and the courtyard. Misfortune.", "Not stepping out of the outer gate and courtyard brings misfortune. Failing to go out when you should means missing the moment."],
    ["He who knows no limitation will have cause to lament. No blame.", "Without restraint you will end up lamenting; but if you can reflect on yourself, there is no blame."],
    ["Contented limitation. Success.", "Being at ease with restraint brings success. You keep within bounds naturally."],
    ["Sweet limitation brings good fortune. Going forth meets with esteem.", "Finding restraint sweet brings good fortune, and going forward wins esteem. Lead by example and take pleasure in it."],
    ["Bitter limitation. Perseverance brings misfortune. Remorse vanishes.", "Finding restraint bitter and clinging to it brings misfortune; if you can repent and correct course, remorse vanishes. Excessive restraint is not advisable either."]
  ],
  61: [
    ["Steadfast in trust: good fortune. With other intentions, there is no ease.", "Keeping quietly to sincerity brings good fortune; harboring other designs leaves you no peace. Stay single-minded."],
    ["A crane calls in the shade; its young answer it. I have a good goblet; I will share it with you.", "A crane calls in the shade of the trees and its young answer in harmony; I have fine wine and wish to share it with you. Sincerity evokes a response, like voices answering one another."],
    ["He finds a counterpart. Now he beats the drum, now he stops; now he weeps, now he sings.", "Meeting an opponent, you now beat the drum to attack, now give up, now weep, now sing. Without inner steadiness, your moods swing unpredictably."],
    ["The moon nearly full. The team horse goes astray. No blame.", "The moon is nearly full and the fine horse leaves its mate. No blame. Give up private factions and devote yourself to what is higher."],
    ["He possesses sincerity, which binds others together. No blame.", "Holding sincerity and being closely bound together: no blame. Use sincerity to unite people's hearts."],
    ["The cry of the rooster rises up to heaven. Perseverance brings misfortune.", "The rooster's crow soars up to heaven; clinging to this brings misfortune. Sound outstrips substance, and empty bluster cannot last."]
  ],
  62: [
    ["The bird meets with misfortune through flying.", "A bird flying up against the current meets misfortune. Flying high beyond your strength."],
    ["Passing by the grandfather, one meets the grandmother. Not reaching the ruler, one meets the minister. No blame.", "Passing by the grandfather, you meet the grandmother; not going beyond the ruler, you meet only the minister. No blame. Keep within proper bounds and settle for the next best thing."],
    ["If he does not take extra care to guard against it, someone may follow and harm him. Misfortune.", "If you refuse to take extra precautions, someone may harm you. Misfortune. Be on guard against petty people."],
    ["No blame. Without overstepping, he meets it. Going forth brings danger; one must be on guard. Do not persist in perseverance for long.", "No blame: without overstepping, you meet just right. Going forward is dangerous and calls for vigilance; do not cling stubbornly to one course for long."],
    ["Dense clouds, no rain, from our western outskirts. The prince shoots and takes the one in the cave.", "Dense clouds gather but no rain falls, drifting in from our western outskirts; the prince shoots and takes what is hidden in the cave. Seek the help of capable people living in seclusion."],
    ["Not meeting it, he goes beyond it. The flying bird is caught in the net. Misfortune. This is called calamity.", "Going too far instead of meeting the mark, like a flying bird caught in a net: misfortune - this is calamity. Going too far is as bad as not going far enough."]
  ],
  63: [
    ["He brakes his wheels. He gets his tail wet. No blame.", "Dragging back the wheels and getting the tail wet: no blame. Just after success, slow down and proceed carefully."],
    ["The woman loses the curtain of her carriage. Do not run after it; on the seventh day it will be found.", "The woman loses her carriage curtain; do not chase after it, for in seven days it will return. No need to force things - what is yours will come in its own time."],
    ["Gaozong attacks Guifang; after three years he conquers it. The petty person must not be employed.", "Gaozong of Yin campaigned against Guifang and took three years to conquer it; petty people must not be employed. Great undertakings require long commitment and careful choice of people."],
    ["For the leak there are rags at hand. Be on guard all day long.", "The boat has a leak, so keep rags ready to plug it and stay on guard all day. In times of safety, do not forget danger."],
    ["The neighbor in the east who slaughters an ox does not attain as much real happiness as the neighbor in the west with his small offering.", "The eastern neighbor who slaughters an ox for a lavish sacrifice receives less true blessing than the western neighbor with a simple offering. Sincerity counts for more than show."],
    ["He gets his head wet. Danger.", "Getting your head wet is dangerous. If you don't know when to stop after success, you will eventually go under."]
  ],
  64: [
    ["He gets his tail wet. Humiliation.", "Getting the tail wet brings regret. Trying to cross the river without enough ability is unlikely to succeed."],
    ["He brakes his wheels. Perseverance brings good fortune.", "Dragging back the wheels: staying upright brings good fortune. Rein in your impatience and build up strength before you move."],
    ["Before completion, going forth brings misfortune. It furthers one to cross the great water.", "The river is not yet crossed and rushing ahead brings misfortune; yet it is favorable to cross the great water (find another route or draw on outside help)."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. Remorse vanishes. Rousing himself, he attacks Guifang; after three years he is rewarded by the great state.", "Staying upright brings good fortune and remorse vanishes. Rising up to campaign against Guifang, after three years you are rewarded by a great state. Long effort pays off in the end."],
    ["Perseverance brings good fortune. No remorse. The light of the superior person; with sincerity, good fortune.", "Staying upright brings good fortune, with no remorse. The radiance of the superior person, treating others with sincerity: good fortune."],
    ["With sincerity, drinking wine. No blame. If he soaks his head, his sincerity loses its measure.", "Drinking wine in celebration with sincerity: no blame. But if you indulge until your head is soaked, even sincerity loses its sense of measure. Don't get carried away when celebrating success."]
  ]
};
